{"event_id": "73739f9b", "event_type": "action", "task_id": "registry-contains-feature--baseline_react--r001", "timestamp": "2026-09-22T15:22:58.908473+00:00", "payload": {"step": 5, "action": {"action_type": "finish", "thought": "", "message": "All 68 tests pass.\n\n## Summary\n\nAdded a `contains(name)` method to `OperationRegistry` in `src/calc_core/registry.py`:\n\n```python\ndef contains(self, name: str) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"Return True if an operation is registered under ``name``.\"\"\"\n    return name in self._operations\n```\n\nThis uses an exact key-membership check against the internal dictionary, so callers can test whether a name is registered without triggering `UnknownOperationError`. The existing `register` and `resolve` methods are unchanged.\n\nVerification: full test suite passes (68 passed).", "tool_call": null}, "raw_content": "All 68 tests pass.\n\n## Summary\n\nAdded a `contains(name)` method to `OperationRegistry` in `src/calc_core/registry.py`:\n\n```python\ndef contains(self, name: str) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"Return True if an operation is registered under ``name``.\"\"\"\n    return name in self._operations\n```\n\nThis uses an exact key-membership check against the internal dictionary, so callers can test whether a name is registered without triggering `UnknownOperationError`. The existing `register` and `resolve` methods are unchanged.\n\nVerification: full test suite passes (68 passed).", "usage": {"input_tokens": 4810, "cached_tokens": 0, "cache_write_tokens": 0, "output_tokens": 135, "reasoning_tokens": 0, "estimated": false, "total_tokens": 4945}, "trace_schema_version": 2, "schema_version": 2, "run_id": "registry-contains-feature--baseline_react--r001_20260922_152228", "run_span_id": "34018a34204041b7", "entrypoint": "eval", "session_id": null, "step_id": 5, "turn_id": "registry-contains-feature--baseline_react--r001_20260922_152228:5", "parent_span_id": "34018a34204041b7"}}
{"event_id": "097f05cd", "event_type": "task_complete", "task_id": "registry-contains-feature--baseline_react--r001", "timestamp": "2026-09-22T15:23:00.212039+00:00", "payload": {"steps": 5, "summary": "All 68 tests pass.\n\n## Summary\n\nAdded a `contains(name)` method to `OperationRegistry` in `src/calc_core/registry.py`:\n\n```python\ndef contains(self, name: str) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"Return True if an operation is registered under ``name``.\"\"\"\n    return name in self._operations\n```\n\nThis uses an exact key-membership check against the internal dictionary, so callers can test whether a name is registered without triggering `UnknownOperationError`. The existing `register` and `resolve` methods are unchanged.\n\nVerification: full test suite passes (68 passed).", "trace_schema_version": 2, "schema_version": 2, "run_id": "registry-contains-feature--baseline_react--r001_20260922_152228", "run_span_id": "34018a34204041b7", "entrypoint": "eval", "session_id": null, "step_id": 5, "turn_id": "registry-contains-feature--baseline_react--r001_20260922_152228:5", "parent_span_id": "34018a34204041b7"}}
